cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, together with the papers it formalizes."
title: "FPPVariance: a Lean 4 formalization of fluctuation bounds for lattice and rotationally invariant first-passage percolation"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of two papers of S.
  Armstrong and A. Bou-Rabee. For first-passage percolation on Z^d, d >= 2,
  with independent, identically distributed weights whose law has an
  exponential moment and mass at zero below the critical probability of bond
  percolation, let xi be a unit vector in R^d, rational or not, at which the
  time constant mu has a positive definite quadratic expansion with a power
  remainder on the orthogonal hyperplane. Then there are epsilon > 0 and C such
  that E exp(|T(0, x) - mu(x)| / (C |x|^((1 - epsilon)/2))) <= 2 for every
  nonzero lattice point x within distance |x|^(3/4) of the ray through xi;
  epsilon and C depend only on the dimension, the law of the weights and the
  constants of this expansion, not on the direction ("Curvature and variance in
  lattice first-passage percolation", Theorem 1.1). The variance bounds that
  follow, Var T(0, x) <= 2 C^2 |x|^(1 - epsilon) for these x and
  Var T(0, floor(n xi)) <= n^(1 - epsilon) for every sufficiently large integer
  n, uniformly in the direction, are proved as well. For the passage time T of a
  rotationally invariant random metric on R^d, d >= 2, whose density is a
  bounded local function of Gaussian white noise or of a homogeneous Poisson
  process and is equivariant under rotations and translations, with time
  constant mu, there are epsilon > 0 and C such that
  E exp(|T(0, x) - mu |x|| / (C |x|^((1 - epsilon)/2))) <= 2 for every point x
  with |x| >= 1 ("Fluctuation bounds for rotationally invariant first-passage
  percolation", Theorems 1.1 and 1.2); the variance bounds that follow,
  Var T(0, t e_1) <= t^(1 - epsilon) for every sufficiently large t and
  Var T(0, x) <= |x|^(1 - epsilon) for every point x with |x| sufficiently
  large, are proved as well. Every result of the literature that the proofs use
  is stated and proved. The proofs use only the standard axioms.
type: software
date-released: 2026-10-31
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
    affiliation: "CNRS & Laboratoire Jacques-Louis Lions, Sorbonne Université and Courant Institute of Mathematical Sciences, New York University"
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, University of Pennsylvania"
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - first-passage percolation
  - random metrics
  - fluctuation bounds
  - variance bounds
  - concentration of measure
license: Apache-2.0
